in N-hydroxylation; CYP2D6, CYP2C19, CYP3A4, and CYP2E1 are considered unlikely to contribute significantly to riluzole metabolism in humans."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00740"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"234.0075"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Riluzole is extensively metabolized to six major and a number of minor metabolites, which have not all been identified to date. Metabolism is mostly hepatic, consisting of cytochrome P450\u0026ndash;dependent hydroxylation and glucuronidation. CYP1A2 is the primary isozyme involved in N-hydroxylation; CYP2D6, CYP2C19, CYP3A4, and CYP2E1 are considered unlikely to contribute significantly to riluzole metabolism in humans."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00741"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"362.2093"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Primarily hepatic via CYP3A4"}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00741"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"362.2093"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Primarily hepatic via CYP3A4"}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00742"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"182.079"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Mannitol is metabolized only slightly, if at all, to glycogen in the liver."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00742"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"182.079"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Mannitol is metabolized only slightly, if at all, to glycogen in the liver."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00744"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"236.0619"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Hepatic. Zileuton and its N-dehydroxylated metabolite are oxidatively metabolized by the cytochrome P450 isoenzymes 1A2, 2C9 and 3A4."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00745"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"273.0823"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Hepatic"}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00746"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"560.3534"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Deferoxamine is mainly metabolised in the plasma and hepatic metabolism is minimal. A number of metabolites have been isolated but not characterised. Some metabolites of deferoxamine, most notably the product of oxidative deamination, also chelate iron, and thus the antidotal effect of the drug appears unaffected by hepatic metabolism."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00746"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"560.3534"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Deferoxamine is mainly metabolised in the plasma and hepatic metabolism is minimal. A number of metabolites have been isolated but not characterised. Some metabolites of deferoxamine, most notably the product of oxidative deamination, also chelate iron, and thus the antidotal effect of the drug appears unaffected by hepatic metabolism."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00747"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"437.1049"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"'null'"}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00748"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"290.1186"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"'null'"}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00748"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"290.1186"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"'null'"}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00749"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"287.1521"},"transform":{"type":"literal","va