s detectable in plasma. Upon in vitro incubation, one of the minor metabolites formed is 6\u0026szlig;-hydroxy-mometasone furoate. In human liver microsomes, the formation of the metabolite is regulated by cytochrome P-450 3A4."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00764"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"426.1365"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Hepatic. Extensive metabolism to multiple metabolites. There are no major metabolites detectable in plasma. Upon in vitro incubation, one of the minor metabolites formed is 6\u0026szlig;-hydroxy-mometasone furoate. In human liver microsomes, the formation of the metabolite is regulated by cytochrome P-450 3A4."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00765"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"195.0895"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Little biotransformation, with catechol metabolites accounting for less than 1% of the administered dose."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00765"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"195.0895"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"Little biotransformation, with catechol metabolites accounting for less than 1% of the administered dose."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00767"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"404.2311"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"'null'"}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00768"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"337.1678"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"The mono-desmethyl and the N-oxide metabolites have been detected at low concentrations in the urine."}},{"drug":{"type":"uri","value":"http://www4.wiwiss.fu-berlin.de/drugbank/resource/drugs/DB00768"},"mass":{"type":"literal","value":"337.1678"},"transform":{"type":"literal","value":"The mono-desmethyl and the N-oxide 